 "text": "-->\nHR | Harper County Kansas\ntop of page\nSkip to Main Content\nHome\nGovernment\nAppraiser\nClerk\nCommissioners\nDept on Aging & Transportation\nElections\nHR\nHealth\nPublic Works\nRegister of Deeds\nTreasurer\nPublic Safety\nAttorney\nDispatch\nDistrict Court\nEMS\nEmergency Management\nSheriff\nCommunity\nChildcare\nEmployment Opportunities\nMore\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nLog In\nHarper County Kansas\nCONTACT US\nUp\nHuman Resources\nLinks\nEmployment Opportunities\nInterested in learning more about working for Harper County?\nEmployment Opportunities\nPolicy and Handbook\nEmployee handbook and policy manual. Updated 02/16/2026\nHandbook and Policy Manual\nHuman Resource Director\nAmi Delacerda\n​\nMy name is Ami (Aleshire) DeLacerda. I was born and raised in Harper County, and am a 1994 graduate of Chaparral High School. In 2016, after 20 years away, I moved back to Anthony to be close to my family. I began working for the county as the Director of Human Resources in October of 2016, bringing over 25 years of experience from similar roles in industries including finance, hospitality, and healthcare.\nMy primary role at the county is to serve as a resource, providing support to current and potential employees and our Board of Commissioners. This includes recruiting and retaining employees, administering payroll and benefits, and implementing county policies and procedures.\nI love being back, serving the community where I grew up, and am passionate about this place and the opportunity I’ve been given to help Harper County remain a wonderful community to work and live in!\nPlease reach out to me if you have any questions about employment with Harper County!\nadelacerda@harpercountyks.gov\nor\n(620)-842-6007\ndocument center\nproperty search\npay taxes\nemployment\ntransportation\n© 2023-24 Harper County, KS -\nbuilt by KanOkla Design Studio\nbottom of page",
